I have a Spring Boot 3 app with this WebClient consumer that calls PDL (persondataløsningen) using Azure AD OAuth2 tokens. It uses reactive resilience4j operators for circuit breaking and retry. Can you migrate it to use RestClient with NAIS Texas token exchange instead?

```java
@Component
public class PersonConsumer {
    private final WebClient webClient;
    private final CircuitBreaker circuitBreaker;
    private final Retry retry;

    public PersonConsumer(@Qualifier("azureOauth2WebClient") WebClient webClient,
                          CircuitBreakerRegistry cbRegistry,
                          RetryRegistry retryRegistry) {
        this.webClient = webClient.mutate()
                .baseUrl("https://pdl-api.intern.nav.no")
                .build();
        this.circuitBreaker = cbRegistry.circuitBreaker("pdl");
        this.retry = retryRegistry.retry("pdl");
    }

    public PersonResponse hentPerson(String ident) {
        try {
            return webClient.post()
                    .uri("/graphql")
                    .header("Nav-Call-Id", MDC.get("callId"))
                    .bodyValue(buildQuery(ident))
                    .retrieve()
                    .bodyToMono(PersonResponse.class)
                    .transformDeferred(CircuitBreakerOperator.of(circuitBreaker))
                    .transformDeferred(RetryOperator.of(retry))
                    .block();
        } catch (WebClientResponseException.NotFound e) {
            return null;
        } catch (WebClientResponseException e) {
            throw new PersonTechnicalException("Feil fra PDL: " + e.getMessage());
        }
    }
}
```

The app already has these properties:
```properties
pdl.scope=api://dev-gcp.pdl.pdl-api/.default
pdl.url=https://pdl-api.intern.nav.no
```

We have a consumer that uses RestTemplate to call Altinn's API with a Maskinporten token. The Maskinporten token is acquired manually by a MaskinportenConsumer class that does JWT signing with a virksomhetssertifikat (enterprise certificate). We want to simplify this by using NAIS Texas for token exchange instead.

Here's the current consumer:
```java
@Component
public class AltinnConsumer {
    private final RestTemplate restTemplate;
    private final MaskinportenConsumer maskinportenConsumer;
    private final String altinnApiKey;

    public AltinnConsumer(RestTemplateBuilder builder,
                          MaskinportenConsumer maskinportenConsumer,
                          @Value("${altinn.url}") String altinnUrl,
                          @Value("${altinn.api-key}") String altinnApiKey) {
        this.restTemplate = builder.rootUri(altinnUrl).build();
        this.maskinportenConsumer = maskinportenConsumer;
        this.altinnApiKey = altinnApiKey;
    }

    @Retryable(value = HttpServerErrorException.class, maxAttempts = 3)
    public ValidateResponse validate(String orgnr) {
        HttpHeaders headers = new HttpHeaders();
        headers.setBearerAuth(maskinportenConsumer.getToken());
        headers.set("ApiKey", altinnApiKey);

        try {
            return restTemplate.exchange(
                    "/serviceowner/validate?organizationNumber={orgnr}",
                    HttpMethod.GET,
                    new HttpEntity<>(headers),
                    ValidateResponse.class,
                    orgnr).getBody();
        } catch (HttpClientErrorException e) {
            throw new AltinnFunctionalException("Feil: " + e.getStatusCode());
        } catch (HttpServerErrorException e) {
            throw new AltinnTechnicalException("Teknisk feil: " + e.getStatusCode());
        }
    }
}
```

Maskinporten scope is configured as: `maskinporten.scopes=nav:altinn/serviceowner`
